---
import DocumentationLayout from '../../layouts/DocumentationLayout.astro';
import {blocks} from '../../data/blocks';
---
<DocumentationLayout title="Blocks" description="Reusable Astro compositions built from DMF UI components." section="blocks">
<h1>Blocks</h1><p class="docs-lead">Compose existing components into native forms and reusable sections. Applications own destinations, data and business logic.</p>
{[...new Set(blocks.map(b=>b.category))].map(category=><section class="docs-section"><h2>{category}</h2><div class="docs-grid">{blocks.filter(b=>b.category===category).map(block=><article class="docs-entry"><a href={`/blocks/${block.slug}/`}>{block.title}</a><p>{block.description}</p></article>)}</div></section>)}
<section class="docs-section docs-prose"><h2>Connected example</h2><p><a href="/examples/discovery/">Merchant discovery</a> connects SearchFiltersBlock, MerchantListingBlock and MerchantCard with URL-backed sample filters, pagination and recovery. <a href="/docs/search-and-recovery/">Search and recovery pattern</a> explains the host boundaries.</p></section>
<section class="docs-section docs-prose"><h2>Composition boundaries</h2><p>Components provide individual controls. Blocks compose repeated structure; Templates define page layouts, and Examples supply product data and workflows. Astro exports all listed Blocks. The separate React alpha implements SignInBlock, SearchFiltersBlock, HeroBlock, MerchantListingBlock and MerchantCard; shared tokens and contracts do not imply a framework-independent rendering runtime.</p><p>SignUpBlock, PasswordRecoveryBlock and PageHeaderBlock remain planned follow-ups. Merchant-detail journeys and product Templates remain planned.</p></section>
</DocumentationLayout>
